{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview","id":817610,"title":"Thoughts on the Beast Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-27T08:12:52-08:00","id":817610,"title":"Thoughts on the Beast Preview","content":"I've been reading the Beasts preview and for some reason part of it just bugs me. It seems to focus a whole lot on being a sexual <b>predatory</b> animal, and less on the whole throwing away your dignity and self-respect from an overriding need to escape by any means. It seems to raw-raw on the whole gleeful abandon of human civility, rather than it being a consequence of throwing away your dignity in the urge to escape. I mean I've read instances where people will do all sorts of insane things to escape confinement, including breaking bones or sawing off their own arms to escape bondage. One specific example that comes to mind is the story of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9hdSLiHaJz8\" target=\"_blank\">Aron Ralston</a>. However, beasts in their current state don't seem like they'd be able to represent such individuals.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm just not getting it, but I do think it could help to focus a little bit more on human base instincts, and less on the sudden development of instincts from entirely separate creatures.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Not to mention, if they're throwing off all the trappings of humanity wholesale, how would they even return to the material world? Why trade one cage for another? It doesn't make a whole lot of sense based on the writing as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-27-2016, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:24:00-08:00","id":817736,"title":"","content":"You should watch this movie to understand it full<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theredlist.com/media/database/muses/icon/cinematic_men/1980/anthony-hopkins/004-anthony-hopkins-theredlist.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/718TQ2DE2TL._SY300_.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:33:57-08:00","id":817745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817736#post817736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should watch this movie to understand it full<br /> <br /> SNIP</div> </div> </div> </div>Really need a [thumb] or [t] tag because that's way too large for my screen.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes I understand that, I will try to watch it (Albeit, I lack funds so it may have to wait). However, the whole aspect of disconnecting yourself from humanity would (seemingly) make you unable to return to it. After all, 1e Changeling said that children that were abducted would never return because they lacked any ties to the material world (Maybe this has changed since then?). So a Beast throwing off pretty much all of their ties to it (in the form of relationships) seems like it'd violate this. Plus, we have an instinct to belong. Did you happen to watch the video I put up discussing psychology? Because I'd think that the idea of <b>family</b> would matter just as much to them. It goes over the whole base needs and sexual needs, but it seems to kind of glaze over our need to socialize. After all, we are a social animal, and our society reflects this. Even in a vacuum we'll sympathize with inanimate objects (The crazy loner on an island talking to a coconut for instance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:42:39-08:00","id":817792,"title":"","content":"1) No. The sexual predator might be easy to see, but it's not all sex, nor is it all predatory. It's screaming in a disorienting fashion to bamboozle the cop getting on you for a jaywalking ticket before running off, it's scratching your itchy crotch in a business meeting with a short skirt on, it's smelling people when you're introduced to them. I wouldn't award the Clarity bonus for all of these, but it's a variety of responses.<br /> <br /> 2) The thing of the matter is that the Beast needs to make choices to remind themselves of how they freed themselves to ground out their sense of being in a sense of what belongs to them. I used animalistic stuff above because it's easy to communicate the idea, but really, the write up <i>does</i> skew towards the human side of taboo-breaking. Really, though, it opens up the range for players to define their characters. There's the punk who disrepects the norms of any sub-culture and place he's in, and there's also the wild man living in the sewers on rats. Beasts can be both.<br /> <br /> 3) The thing to remember is that paranoia of being captured is, as a norm, higher than the risk of actually being captured. THe divide between the two is smaller than in first edition, but for the most part, as a psychological horror game, the simple fact is that the fairies are going to come less for you than you think they will, because the dread of them coming is one of the biggest emotional drives of the game.<br /> <br /> With this in mind, the Blessings aren't about flight responses, not exclusively, but rather tapping into the archetype of the moment you freed yourself to remind yourself that you have power over your own life. It's not about giving into the lizard-brain to run away, it's about indulging in the base to remind yourself that you aren't as restrained as you think you are. It's being unafraid of touching shit because the key is hidden in it and being okay with crying in public, even in Japan*, because fuck it, you need to cry. It's about being yourself, even when circumstances tell you the particulars of such is inappropriate for modern civilization.<br /> <br /> 4)That said, it's an exercise of archetype, not a way of life. A Beast is not compelled to flaunt the niceities all the time. A Beast can go to the five-star restaurant and go all night without digging into the meal with hands and face or finger her date behind the table or anything-the Beast can honestly just have a nice, elegant evening. The Clarity Blessing is more a personalized focus for when the Clarity attacks come in. Going back to a Jessica Jones reference, it's the Beast going reciting street names from their childhood home area. You don't do it all the time. You do it when you really need to get your Clarity back up.<br /> <br /> *Especially if you're not drunk!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:22:06-08:00","id":817826,"title":"","content":"The Beast is about reclaiming agency by being defiant against rules. Changelings are people who've suffered a lot, and they try to get a grip in ways that may not be socially acceptable but are nonetheless psychologically healthy for them. Beasts break societal rules because it's a convenient way of reminding themselves of that time where they broke the Gentry's rules and reclaimed their agency and freedom.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't judge them. They don't do anything actually harmful and they're just trying to cope the best they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:30:29-08:00","id":817832,"title":"","content":"I look at it as not of abandoning people or connections, but of abandoning the more restrictive or &quot;unnecessarily&quot; complicated social rules of society. A Beast still wants friends and will act to protect them, but they're disinclined to play by the labyrinthine rules of polite society, especially when those rules get in the way of a simple, pragmatic method.<br /> <br /> Table manners: &quot;Why should I bother with the difference between all those forks? In fact, why should I use forks when I've got perfectly good hands?&quot;<br /> Sex: &quot;Why all the complicated emotions, jealousy, marriage, and so on? I'm hot, you're hot. Can't we just <i>do it</i>?&quot;<br /> Combat: &quot;Why can't I fight dirty or hit below the belt? This is a fight, not a game of checkers!&quot;<br /> Clothing: &quot;I'm too sexy for my shirt. And shoes. Therefore, I can do without your service.&quot;<br /> Tact: &quot;Why can't I just blurt out what we're all thinking instead of dancing around the elephant in the room?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the inner conflict Beasts have that makes it harder to simply disappear in the crowd of humanity. They get a stronger feeling of identity and agency by cutting through the social red tape because it echoes their escape and the feeling of liberation that came with it. It's not about becoming anti-social, it's about defying the social conventions that don't make sense or have no immediately recognizable purpose or benefit. They might look at some rules as being too reminiscent of the irrational rules their Keeper imposed on them. They might see some social rules as unjust laws tyrants use to keep their power and keep the common people unwilling to stand up for themselves because it'd be 'impolite' or subject them to public shaming. They might see social rules used as excuses to avoid thinking and thus lose agency in your own actions. Sometimes they might break rules just to prove to themselves that they're acting on their own, instead of just caving into the will of the public or of authority figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:52:12-08:00","id":817856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817826#post817826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast is about reclaiming agency by being defiant against rules. Changelings are people who've suffered a lot, and they try to get a grip in ways that may not be socially acceptable but are nonetheless psychologically healthy for them. Beasts break societal rules because it's a convenient way of reminding themselves of that time where they broke the Gentry's rules and reclaimed their agency and freedom.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't judge them. They don't do anything actually harmful and they're just trying to cope the best they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you are getting at, but I don't know if beasts (as written) really get the point across. I do like the whole angle of &quot;Prisons can be made of more than crude stone and metal&quot; but I don't feel that Beast really focuses on that realization, instead favoring a more typical acting out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817792#post817792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) No. The sexual predator might be easy to see, but it's not all sex, nor is it all predatory. It's screaming in a disorienting fashion to bamboozle the cop getting on you for a jaywalking ticket before running off, it's scratching your itchy crotch in a business meeting with a short skirt on, it's smelling people when you're introduced to them. I wouldn't award the Clarity bonus for all of these, but it's a variety of responses.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that the text constantly makes allusions to predator. &quot;You are a shark&quot; or &quot;You look like a lion&quot; and other things like that. I think it muddles things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817792#post817792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The thing of the matter is that the Beast needs to make choices to remind themselves of how they freed themselves to ground out their sense of being in a sense of what belongs to them. I used animalistic stuff above because it's easy to communicate the idea, but really, the write up <i>does</i> skew towards the human side of taboo-breaking. Really, though, it opens up the range for players to define their characters. There's the punk who disrepects the norms of any sub-culture and place he's in, and there's also the wild man living in the sewers on rats. Beasts can be both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I see is that it doesn't really get it's message across. I guess the message should be a realization of &quot;what really matters&quot; rather than &quot;I acted out therefore I am free.&quot; Because it seems to focus a lot on the latter and not a whole like the former.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817792#post817792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The thing to remember is that paranoia of being captured is, as a norm, higher than the risk of actually being captured. THe divide between the two is smaller than in first edition, but for the most part, as a psychological horror game, the simple fact is that the fairies are going to come less for you than you think they will, because the dread of them coming is one of the biggest emotional drives of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand that. Albeit the Huntsman in their current form kind of undermine that with their two-week timer, but that's another discussion for another time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817792#post817792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this in mind, the Blessings aren't about flight responses, not exclusively, but rather tapping into the archetype of the moment you freed yourself to remind yourself that you have power over your own life. It's not about giving into the lizard-brain to run away, it's about indulging in the base to remind yourself that you aren't as restrained as you think you are. It's being unafraid of touching shit because the key is hidden in it and being okay with crying in public, even in Japan*, because fuck it, you need to cry. It's about being yourself, even when circumstances tell you the particulars of such is inappropriate for modern civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand that. However, it almost entirely focuses on the archetype and only has a sentence or two that really puts the flight into perspective. At least, that's what I took away from the way it's written. Hence why I am bringing this up. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817832#post817832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I look at it as not of abandoning people or connections, but of abandoning the more restrictive or &quot;unnecessarily&quot; complicated social rules of society. A Beast still wants friends and will act to protect them, but they're disinclined to play by the labyrinthine rules of polite society, especially when those rules get in the way of a simple, pragmatic method.<br /> <br /> Table manners: &quot;Why should I bother with the difference between all those forks? In fact, why should I use forks when I've got perfectly good hands?&quot;<br /> Sex: &quot;Why all the complicated emotions, jealousy, marriage, and so on? I'm hot, you're hot. Can't we just <i>do it</i>?&quot;<br /> Combat: &quot;Why can't I fight dirty or hit below the belt? This is a fight, not a game of checkers!&quot;<br /> Clothing: &quot;I'm too sexy for my shirt. And shoes. Therefore, I can do without your service.&quot;<br /> Tact: &quot;Why can't I just blurt out what we're all thinking instead of dancing around the elephant in the room?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the inner conflict Beasts have that makes it harder to simply disappear in the crowd of humanity. They get a stronger feeling of identity and agency by cutting through the social red tape because it echoes their escape and the feeling of liberation that came with it. It's not about becoming anti-social, it's about defying the social conventions that don't make sense or have no immediately recognizable purpose or benefit. They might look at some rules as being too reminiscent of the irrational rules their Keeper imposed on them. They might see some social rules as unjust laws tyrants use to keep their power and keep the common people unwilling to stand up for themselves because it'd be 'impolite' or subject them to public shaming. They might see social rules used as excuses to avoid thinking and thus lose agency in your own actions. Sometimes they might break rules just to prove to themselves that they're acting on their own, instead of just caving into the will of the public or of authority figures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yes, I understand and I get that. I just don't think beasts communicate that effectively in it's draft state. Too much focus on rebelling from societal norms and less on focusing on the base human instincts. Basically, the more about why they do it, not the fact that they do it. I would definitely want to see some more fear and fight-or-flight aspects put into it, because right now it seems all fight and rebelling which doesn't seem like it'd make a whole lot of sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> PS. Did anyone actually watch the video I put in the OP? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:58:46-08:00","id":817873,"title":"","content":"1) Predators are easier to sell. More people think of them as cool, and what's more, it's fun to sell the edge of a character type when they're dangerous.That doesn't stop prey from happening.<br /> <br /> 2) Not everyone instantly gets a Huntsman on them. True Fae generally wait to see if a toy is interesting enough to keep their attention after leaving but difficult enough that the Loyalists and Fetch can't do anything about them.<br /> <br /> I'm heading out soon, so the rest'll come later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:04:34-08:00","id":817885,"title":"","content":"The problem with your example of Ralston is that he's not a Beast. That's where you're getting mixed up. Ralston is a Wizened. He shed the parts of himself that were keeping him trapped, did so through sheer ingenuity, and then later on, probably replaced his arm with prosthetics. It's true, Beasts don't reflect the Ralston story very well, but the Wizened do.<br /> <br /> I agree the text could do better than to try and sell yet another example of a beast-like predator (when we already have Vampire and Beast), but honestly, it feels like a very minor quibble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:20:26-08:00","id":817895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817885#post817885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with your example of Ralston is that he's not a Beast. That's where you're getting mixed up. Ralston is a Wizened. He shed the parts of himself that were keeping him trapped, did so through sheer ingenuity, and then later on, probably replaced his arm with prosthetics. It's true, Beasts don't reflect the Ralston story very well, but the Wizened do.<br /> <br /> I agree the text could do better than to try and sell yet another example of a beast-like predator (when we already have Vampire and Beast), but honestly, it feels like a very minor quibble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Because when I think of the imagery I see a creature with an overriding desire to escape by any means, even at the cost of life and limb. Like an animal with it's leg in a trap willing to gnaw off it's own leg to escape. I see that the direct imagery for the Wizened <b>sound</b> similar, but the meat of it doesn't seem to fit. It's less about the instincts and more about the craft. Whereas in the example with Ralston it's an overriding instinct or motivation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Again this may be bad reading on my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-27-2016, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:39:21-08:00","id":817908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817895#post817895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Because when I think of the imagery I see a creature with an overriding desire to escape by any means, even at the cost of life and limb. Like an animal with it's leg in a trap willing to gnaw off it's own leg to escape. I see that the direct imagery for the Wizened <b>sound</b> similar, but the meat of it doesn't seem to fit. It's less about the instincts and more about the craft. Whereas in the example with Ralston it's an overriding instinct or motivation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Again this may be bad reading on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>The video describes the survival instincts common in all mankind, so it's not like it will resonate more specifically with one Seeming over any other.<br /> <br /> Ralston is a difficult example to translate into Changeling because his circumstances were a result of accident, rather than deliberate intent. The Gentry don't kidnap people at random and then leave them wherever, each changeling was taken for a purpose. So let's just say that doppel-Ralston's purpose was to suffer for his Keeper's amusement. His arm was pinned with a rock and he was forced to find ways to subsist. The videotaping angle can be a Keeper's trick to get him to suffer even more, so we'll run with that. Let's examine how each Seeming would free themselves (minus Darkling and Fairest, who usually need another changeling present in order to coalesce):<br /> <br /> Beast: &quot;He wants me to suffer. It's the unspoken rule. Do what I want and you might make it out. Entertain me and you may live. Dance for me, little monkey. So fuck that. I'm not your pet.&quot; Doppel-Ralston becomes stoic. When the Keeper goes to tinker with the stone pinning him, thinking he needs to make things more difficult to elicit a response from his captive, doppel-Ralston breaks free with startling quickness.<br /> Elemental: &quot;I can't blame the rock. It's just doing what it was meant to do. I'm the problem, fighting against things that I can't change.&quot; Doppel-Ralston closes his eyes and focuses on the rock. He draws strength from its stability and constancy. When he opens his eyes again, he's become one with the rock. Unseen, he escapes.<br /> Ogre: &quot;This is violence against me. He's using the rock for it, but it's violence nonetheless. I'm sick of it. He wants pain? I'll give him pain.&quot; Doppel-Ralston quietly seethes with fury until he can't take it anymore. One night, he loses it completely and punches the rock into fragments, harming himself in the process but reclaiming his freedom.<br /> Wizened: &quot;It's my body that's to blame. Too weak. Too fragile. I should know better than this. I can get myself out, if I can just figure out how.&quot; Doppel-Ralston contemplates, calculates, runs mental simulations. He eventually realises his arm is the weakest spot. It has to go. But it's okay. He can remake it, better, so that it doesn't happen again.<br /> <br /> Does that help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:20:42-08:00","id":817953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817908#post817908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The video describes the survival instincts common in all mankind, so it's not like it will resonate more specifically with one Seeming over any other.<br /> <br /> Ralston is a difficult example to translate into Changeling because his circumstances were a result of accident, rather than deliberate intent. The Gentry don't kidnap people at random and then leave them wherever, each changeling was taken for a purpose. So let's just say that doppel-Ralston's purpose was to suffer for his Keeper's amusement. His arm was pinned with a rock and he was forced to find ways to subsist. The videotaping angle can be a Keeper's trick to get him to suffer even more, so we'll run with that. Let's examine how each Seeming would free themselves (minus Darkling and Fairest, who usually need another changeling present in order to coalesce):<br /> <br /> Beast: &quot;He wants me to suffer. It's the unspoken rule. Do what I want and you might make it out. Entertain me and you may live. Dance for me, little monkey. So fuck that. I'm not your pet.&quot; Doppel-Ralston becomes stoic. When the Keeper goes to tinker with the stone pinning him, thinking he needs to make things more difficult to elicit a response from his captive, doppel-Ralston breaks free with startling quickness.<br /> Elemental: &quot;I can't blame the rock. It's just doing what it was meant to do. I'm the problem, fighting against things that I can't change.&quot; Doppel-Ralston closes his eyes and focuses on the rock. He draws strength from its stability and constancy. When he opens his eyes again, he's become one with the rock. Unseen, he escapes.<br /> Ogre: &quot;This is violence against me. He's using the rock for it, but it's violence nonetheless. I'm sick of it. He wants pain? I'll give him pain.&quot; Doppel-Ralston quietly seethes with fury until he can't take it anymore. One night, he loses it completely and punches the rock into fragments, harming himself in the process but reclaiming his freedom.<br /> Wizened: &quot;It's my body that's to blame. Too weak. Too fragile. I should know better than this. I can get myself out, if I can just figure out how.&quot; Doppel-Ralston contemplates, calculates, runs mental simulations. He eventually realises his arm is the weakest spot. It has to go. But it's okay. He can remake it, better, so that it doesn't happen again.<br /> <br /> Does that help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if I remember in 1e it says sometimes people just find themselves in the hedge and &quot;disappear.&quot; So it's not exactly impossible to end up in the keeper's hands by accident.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd have thought that base instincts like that would be what makes a Beast a Beast, but I guess that's not true. So that leaves me rather confused as to what Beast is supposed to be. At any rate, those are interesting though the Wizened one never really seemed to fit quite right. It's too focused on a skill so it doesn't quite make sense (at least from my perspective). Again, it's probably me not getting the brilliance behind it.<br /> <br /> <br /> That does make me think though, could there be a seeming for boring the Gentry to the point where they throw you out? Eg. Like the Dark Lords throwing out Lord Soth from Ravenloft, because no matter what they did they couldn't get a reaction, neither through punishment nor hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:58:34-08:00","id":818023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817953#post817953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, if I remember in 1e it says sometimes people just find themselves in the hedge and &quot;disappear.&quot; So it's not exactly impossible to end up in the keeper's hands by accident.<br /> <br /> I'd have thought that base instincts like that would be what makes a Beast a Beast, but I guess that's not true. So that leaves me rather confused as to what Beast is supposed to be. At any rate, those are interesting though the Wizened one never really seemed to fit quite right. It's too focused on a skill so it doesn't quite make sense (at least from my perspective). Again, it's probably me not getting the brilliance behind it.<br /> <br /> That does make me think though, could there be a seeming for boring the Gentry to the point where they throw you out? Eg. Like the Dark Lords throwing out Lord Soth from Ravenloft, because no matter what they did they couldn't get a reaction, neither through punishment nor hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you find yourself in the Hedge, in order for you to have a Seeming, you must have been taken prisoner by one of the Gentry (which implies you are given a purpose), so my point still stands. If you wander into the Hedge and then find your way out, that seems more of a Fae-Touched thing to me. And even if you became a changeling, a lack of agency would make you Seemingless.<br /> <br /> It's not base instincts, it's the defiance of societal norms. It evokes the idea of a &quot;pet&quot; that refuses to be tamed, that bites the hand that abuses it. In psychological terms, the Beast deals with trauma by reasserting their own power and identity through the defiance of mores. It's not about being animalistic, it's about refusing to play ball. Beasts see the myriad rules of politeness and the convoluted societal mores as traps that remind them of Arcadia. Again, I bring up the <i>Gentry</i>, thinly veiled metaphor for the high class, etc.<br /> <br /> If you do not have agency (that is, if they throw you out as opposed to them letting you out because you became a Loyalist), you do not get a Seeming. A Seeming is the way the changeling rises from Victim to Survivor. A discarded Victim is still a Victim.<br /> <br /> If you want a changeling that rises above the pain through sheer stoicism and transcends their mere self in the process, that's the Elemental Seeming. But they still escape, they don't get thrown out. They just drift away through the earth/clouds/water/magma until they find their way out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:18:37-08:00","id":818032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=817953#post817953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have thought that base instincts like that would be what makes a Beast a Beast, but I guess that's not true. So that leaves me rather confused as to what Beast is supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The beast is breaking the social convention and social expectation. So personally I think instead of &quot;He wants me to suffer. It's the unspoken rule. Do what I want and you might make it out. Entertain me and you may live. Dance for me, little monkey. So fuck that. I'm not your pet. Doppel-Ralston becomes stoic.&quot; it would be &quot;He wants me to suffer. It's the unspoken rule. Do what I want and you might make it out. Entertain me and you may live. Dance for me, little monkey. So fuck that. I'm not your pet. Doppel-Ralston starts to enjoy the pain rather than suffer through it.&quot; <br /> <br /> Beast is being a noble class person, and acting like a peasant. It's using the wrong fork up to 11.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:24:28-08:00","id":818035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818023#post818023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not base instincts, it's the defiance of societal norms. It evokes the idea of a &quot;pet&quot; that refuses to be tamed, that bites the hand that abuses it. In psychological terms, the Beast deals with trauma by reasserting their own power and identity through the defiance of mores. It's not about being animalistic, it's about refusing to play ball. Beasts see the myriad rules of politeness and the convoluted societal mores as traps that remind them of Arcadia. Again, I bring up the <i>Gentry</i>, thinly veiled metaphor for the high class, etc.<br /> <br /> If you do not have agency (that is, if they throw you out as opposed to them letting you out because you became a Loyalist), you do not get a Seeming. A Seeming is the way the changeling rises from Victim to Survivor. A discarded Victim is still a Victim.<br /> <br /> If you want a changeling that rises above the pain through sheer stoicism and transcends their mere self in the process, that's the Elemental Seeming. But they still escape, they don't get thrown out. They just drift away through the earth/clouds/water/magma until they find their way out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, beasts are all about the rebel culture. Okay, guess that explains why it's all about the predator terminology (Because everyone else is sheeple, WAKE UP). Oh well, that's rather disappointing. So there's not <b>really</b> a seeming that references base human instincts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:37:11-08:00","id":818043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818032#post818032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beast is breaking the social convention and social expectation. So personally I think instead of &quot;He wants me to suffer. It's the unspoken rule. Do what I want and you might make it out. Entertain me and you may live. Dance for me, little monkey. So fuck that. I'm not your pet. Doppel-Ralston becomes stoic.&quot; it would be &quot;He wants me to suffer. It's the unspoken rule. Do what I want and you might make it out. Entertain me and you may live. Dance for me, little monkey. So fuck that. I'm not your pet. Doppel-Ralston starts to enjoy the pain rather than suffer through it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast is being a noble class person, and acting like a peasant. It's using the wrong fork up to 11.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is value is making Beasts more nuanced and diverse than that. IMO refusing to play by the rules by displaying defiant stoicism is a Beast-like trait, and could be reflected in big, powerful animals like elephants, rhinos, whales and bears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818035#post818035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, beasts are all about the rebel culture. Okay, guess that explains why it's all about the predator terminology (Because everyone else is sheeple, WAKE UP). Oh well, that's rather disappointing. So there's not <b>really</b> a seeming that references base human instincts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seemings are about agency. Every Seeming makes a choice when they escape. The Fairest and the Darkling sacrifice (the Fairest themselves, the Darkling someone else). The Elemental lets go of their sense of self. The Ogre lashes out. The Wizened outsmarts. The Beast defies/subverts.<br /> <br /> &quot;Base human instinct&quot; is not really a choice, it's an impulse. There's little agency involved in that. You could spin it as an Elemental-like surrendering to their primal self, and perhaps become some sort of nature elemental, that's about as close as you're going to get to what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:46:06-08:00","id":818047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818043#post818043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there is value is making Beasts more nuanced and diverse than that. IMO refusing to play by the rules by displaying defiant stoicism is a Beast-like trait, and could be reflected in big, powerful animals like elephants, rhinos, whales and bears.<br /> <br /> Seemings are about agency. Every Seeming makes a choice when they escape. The Fairest and the Darkling sacrifice (the Fairest themselves, the Darkling someone else). The Elemental lets go of their sense of self. The Ogre lashes out. The Wizened outsmarts. The Beast defies/subverts.<br /> <br /> &quot;Base human instinct&quot; is not really a choice, it's an impulse. There's little agency involved in that. You could spin it as an Elemental-like surrendering to their primal self, and perhaps become some sort of nature elemental, that's about as close as you're going to get to what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is that all of the seemings involve, ultimately, defying your keeper. So where does that put Beasts? &quot;None of the above?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:50:34-08:00","id":818051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818047#post818047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is that all of the seemings involve, ultimately, defying your keeper. So where does that put Beasts? &quot;None of the above?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That puts the Beasts at &quot;the act of defiance internalizes the fact of defiance.&quot;<br /> <br /> For the other seemings, the fact that they're defying their Keeper by escaping is incidental to the fact that they are escaping; Beasts escape <i>by</i> defying the strictures of their Keeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:50:34-08:00","id":818052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818047#post818047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is that all of the seemings involve, ultimately, defying your keeper. So where does that put Beasts? &quot;None of the above?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say &quot;subversion.&quot; The Beast subverts a rule that they are expected to obey. This subversion is what stuns/distracts/outrages their Keeper and allows them to escape. It's a calculated move meant to startle and wrongfoot the Gentry, and that's why the Beast regains Clarity for doing something socially unacceptable. That moment of stunned disbelief you have when you see a woman eating with her hands instead of knife and fork is what restores the Beast's Clarity, because the Keeper experienced a similar stunned reaction and that's what allowed the Beast to escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:02:28-08:00","id":818063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818043#post818043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is value is making Beasts more nuanced and diverse than that. IMO refusing to play by the rules by displaying defiant stoicism is a Beast-like trait, and could be reflected in big, powerful animals like elephants, rhinos, whales and bears.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really break the expectation though. Toughing it out or suffering are two expected results. There is nothing subversive about them, so I don't see how stoicism works in this &quot;specific&quot; example (other situations I can easily see stoicism leading to beast though).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:06:19-08:00","id":818068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818063#post818063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't really break the expectation though. Toughing it out or suffering are two expected results. There is nothing subversive about them, so I don't see how stoicism works in this &quot;specific&quot; example (other situations I can easily see stoicism leading to beast though).</div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly becoming stoic after you've given into the suffering is a form of defiance. You are deliberately saying &quot;I am aware of what you want from me and I'm going to stop giving it to you.&quot; I completely agree that if you <i>start</i> by toughing it out, then it's no longer a subversion or defiance. But a prisoner that was willing to cry and plead yesterday suddenly becoming stony will give the Keeper pause, and that's when the changeling pounces upon the chance to escape. To me, the essence of the Beast's defiance is when they do something that genuinely stuns the Keeper, at least for a moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:10:46-08:00","id":818072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818068#post818068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Suddenly becoming stoic after you've given into the suffering is a form of defiance. You are deliberately saying &quot;I am aware of what you want from me and I'm going to stop giving it to you.&quot; I completely agree that if you <i>start</i> by toughing it out, then it's no longer a subversion or defiance. But a prisoner that was willing to cry and plead yesterday suddenly becoming stony will give the Keeper pause, and that's when the changeling pounces upon the chance to escape. To me, the essence of the Beast's defiance is when they do something that genuinely stuns the Keeper, at least for a moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair enough, I misunderstood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:47:21-08:00","id":818093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818051#post818051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That puts the Beasts at &quot;the act of defiance internalizes the fact of defiance.&quot;<br /> <br /> For the other seemings, the fact that they're defying their Keeper by escaping is incidental to the fact that they are escaping; Beasts escape <i>by</i> defying the strictures of their Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that makes sense, kinda. Don't see how I could go about playing one though. Oh well, seems like I'm destined to dislike anything that has the word &quot;beast&quot; in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:59:57-08:00","id":818101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818093#post818093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that makes sense, kinda. Don't see how I could go about playing one though. Oh well, seems like I'm destined to dislike anything that has the word &quot;beast&quot; in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I played a Beast, I'd probably make it a social justice warrior type that questions the patriarchy, heterosexism, ableism and the like. A bit heavy-handed, but it works.<br /> <br /> Society has problematic mores and you can absolutely make a heroic Beast that actively defies and shocks those that would uphold them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:16:41-08:00","id":818111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818101#post818101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I played a Beast, I'd probably make it a social justice warrior type that questions the patriarchy, heterosexism, ableism and the like. A bit heavy-handed, but it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm cringing already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:27:24-08:00","id":818116,"title":"","content":"Hey, characters don't have to be perfect. I often make characters that are deeply flawed to start with, and then keep in mind how they're going to overcome those flaws and develop as characters. I think an important theme of Beast Changelings is that defying society too much puts you on the fringe. It makes you the lonely hedge witch in the woods, the hermit in the cave. Part of their character growth is realising that you can't just constantly snub society and shock people, sometimes you need to do a bit of tit for tat with society in order to get what you want. How much compromise is too much is, of course, where the interesting bits lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:41:00-08:00","id":818119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818116#post818116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, characters don't have to be perfect. I often make characters that are deeply flawed to start with, and then keep in mind how they're going to overcome those flaws and develop as characters. I think an important theme of Beast Changelings is that defying society too much puts you on the fringe. It makes you the lonely hedge witch in the woods, the hermit in the cave. Part of their character growth is realising that you can't just constantly snub society and shock people, sometimes you need to do a bit of tit for tat with society in order to get what you want. How much compromise is too much is, of course, where the interesting bits lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows, since it is OPP that's probably exactly how they're supposed to be played. The word Beast makes me think feral, not as in Rebel. So I guess I'm a bit tainted by my bias in that regard. Oh well, hopefully there will be other seemings that don't have such of a negative subculture associated with it, hopefully. I was more hoping Beasts would resemble Feral Children, but it seems like I was mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:53:06-08:00","id":818128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818119#post818119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who knows, since it is OPP that's probably exactly how they're supposed to be played. The word Beast makes me think feral, not as in Rebel. So I guess I'm a bit tainted by my bias in that regard. Oh well, hopefully there will be other seemings that don't have such of a negative subculture associated with it, hopefully. I was more hoping Beasts would resemble Feral Children, but it seems like I was mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Ogre or Elemental Seemings + a &quot;feral&quot; Kith is what you're looking for. Seemings are not about aesthetics (though they influence it), they're about philosophy and psychology. If you are focused on an aesthetic idea of a feral changeling, start with the Kith and go from there.<br /> <br /> I also think that Changeling's tone is <i>drastically</i> different from, say, Vampire's, so negative subcultures are less problematic, since the idea that your character is going to grow and overcome their flaws and become a better person is sort of implicit in the whole deal about the Wyrd and Arcadia running on narrative rules. The way I see it, changelings fresh out of Arcadia would have flaws aplenty that they'd later resolve for character growth, which in turn would increase their Wyrd and other assorted powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T19:24:46-08:00","id":818145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818093#post818093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that makes sense, kinda. Don't see how I could go about playing one though. Oh well, seems like I'm destined to dislike anything that has the word &quot;beast&quot; in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, a beast only has to break the expectations during their escape. I had a changeling who was used as a living NPC for a Gentry, so that he and his allies could enthrall themselves in the new story medium of tabletop gaming, but one day he defied the gentry and made himself a PC and ended up earning his freedom by breaking the expectations and the narrative chains that were upon him. This resulted in him being a Beast Mirrorskin once he escaped. But once he got out he did not then just change his personality and start acting out against all social expectation just because of his seeming, but he did try to standout more and actually do what he wants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The word Beast makes me think feral, not as in Rebel </div> </div> </div>Same here actually. To me, it's being You. Not what other people think. Your not rebelling, your just going off who you are instinctively rather than being shackled up by other people and their expectations. You don't do something because your &quot;fighting the power&quot;, you do it because your a beast and you do what your instincts tell you to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-27-2016, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T19:30:13-08:00","id":818148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818128#post818128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Ogre or Elemental Seemings + a &quot;feral&quot; Kith is what you're looking for. Seemings are not about aesthetics (though they influence it), they're about philosophy and psychology. If you are focused on an aesthetic idea of a feral changeling, start with the Kith and go from there.<br /> <br /> I also think that Changeling's tone is <i>drastically</i> different from, say, Vampire's, so negative subcultures are less problematic, since the idea that your character is going to grow and overcome their flaws and become a better person is sort of implicit in the whole deal about the Wyrd and Arcadia running on narrative rules. The way I see it, changelings fresh out of Arcadia would have flaws aplenty that they'd later resolve for character growth, which in turn would increase their Wyrd and other assorted powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, how isn't being a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feral_child\" target=\"_blank\">feral child</a> psychology? The thing is that I guess I don't follow how someone goes from being screwed over by the Gentry to social justice warrior. The two tones seem to conflict quite heavily. Beast seems to be trying to pander to &quot;primal reversion&quot; and &quot;angsty rebel&quot; simultaneously and I don't really think it fits. Maybe it's not really trying to be the formal at all, but it certainly tries to pretend it is. I don't even know why they're called Beasts anyway, doesn't seem to really fit what they're supposed to be.<br /> <br /> I guess the problem with the tone is there's a difference between <b>ignoring</b> cultural norms, and actively <b>spitting in the face</b> of cultural norms. Beasts, in their current state, seem to do the latter. It's almost some mix of preachy and rebelling without a cause, and it really rubs me the wrong way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818145#post818145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, a beast only has to break the expectations during their escape. I had a changeling who was used as a living NPC for a Gentry, so that he and his allies could enthrall themselves in the new story medium of tabletop gaming, but one day he defied the gentry and made himself a PC and ended up earning his freedom by breaking the expectations and the narrative chains that were upon him. This resulted in him being a Beast Mirrorskin once he escaped. But once he got out he did not then just change his personality and start acting out against all social expectation just because of his seeming, but he did try to standout more and actually do what he wants.<br /> <br /> Same here actually. To me, it's being You. Not what other people think. Your not rebelling, your just going off who you are instinctively rather than being shackled up by other people and their expectations. You don't do something because your &quot;fighting the power&quot;, you do it because your a beast and you do what your instincts tell you to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I'm bringing this up, I think maybe it should be reevaluated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-27-2016, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T19:46:51-08:00","id":818159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818148#post818148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, how isn't being a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feral_child\" target=\"_blank\">feral child</a> psychology?</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be overly focused on the aesthetic idea of a feral child, since you are associating the Beast Seeming with it, when the only thing they both have in common is the appeal to wildness. The psychology of a Beast does not match the feral children. Like I said before, try Ogre or Elemental instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818148#post818148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that I guess I don't follow how someone goes from being screwed over by the Gentry to social justice warrior. The two tones seem to conflict quite heavily. Beast seems to be trying to pander to &quot;primal reversion&quot; and &quot;angsty rebel&quot; simultaneously and I don't really think it fits. Maybe it's not really trying to be the formal at all, but it certainly tries to pretend it is. I don't even know why they're called Beasts anyway, doesn't seem to really fit what they're supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem is that you're overly limiting and restricting character concepts to rigid stereotypes, and don't allow sufficient leeway for things to actually make sense. If your Keeper was a stereotypical patriarchal great white hunter, then you might see shades of him whenever a rich older white man speaks on TV. It makes quite a bit of sense if you are willing to imagine the situation and allow it to unfold to its logical conclusion instead of just fixating on a single specific thing and expecting everything to revolve around it. Not all Beasts are overtly feral or predatory. Some of them are skittish and fast, some are big and majestic, some are sleek and elegant, some are sharp and ornery, some are gentle until roused, and so on. The thing they all have in common is that they regain Clarity when they defy societal conventions, because it evokes how they escaped.<br /> <br /> Even the current text doesn't always reference predators or feral changelings. One of the examples is a changeling that digs his way out of his kennel. That's very non-confrontative, and yet it's also a defiance of social norms. You're not supposed to dig your way out of a cage. You're supposed to stay in there like the good tamed pet you are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818148#post818148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the problem with the tone is there's a difference between <b>ignoring</b> cultural norms, and actively <b>spitting in the face</b> of cultural norms. Beasts, in their current state, seem to do the latter. It's almost some mix of preachy and rebelling without a cause, and it really rubs me the wrong way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's fair or reasonable of you to expect all Beast changelings to behave the same way and have the same opinions regarding societal mores. Some may be happy merely ignoring them (some may do so rarely, others constantly), some may want to actively spit in the face of them. It's character diversity, and it's a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818148#post818148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I'm bringing this up, I think maybe it should be reevaluated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would tone down the predator references (done to death in Vampire, Werewolf and Beast), but other than that, I think the core concept of Beast is absolutely perfect and I think it should be merely diversified rather than reevaluated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T19:47:37-08:00","id":818160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818148#post818148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I'm bringing this up, I think maybe it should be reevaluated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got my interpretation from the preview though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T20:53:56-08:00","id":818181,"title":"","content":"Figure I might as well bring up my character concept for Ziggy Zapf for critique, since it's appropriate to this thread.<br /> <br /> Abduction and Durance: He was a game developer stuck in development hell caused by numerous conflicts. The game he wanted to design was a survival experience where the player controls a pack of magical beasts resembling those in collectible monster games. His Keeper offered him a way to make his game &quot;come alive.&quot; He didn't realize how literal the deal was. He winds up as a disembodied game warden, allegedly impartial referee, managing a version of his game twisted to bloodsport.<br /> <br /> Escape: His Keeper often threatened to punish him by turning him into one of the monsters and forcing him to fight for his survival. After preparations, he manages to set up circumstances so that he can essentially customize his monster body, and contrary to his Keeper's expectations, he focused entirely on running, seeing no dignity in going down in &quot;honorable&quot; combat. He used his knowledge of the game, stealth, and so forth to reach an exit he put in a briar patch. Suddenly having a body again was exhilarating, especially one that he modified himself, and its athletic ability served him well in the realm's ever-shifting terrain.<br /> <br /> The inner conflict: Ziggy was always an intellectual type, but his Durance and escape gave him a deep appreciation for his physical side. When not attending to formal matters, he often wears as little clothing as possible, to the point that he writes his best computer code in the buff. Additionally, while he still likes being connected with the human world, he has little attachment to the &quot;pure&quot; human form: He enjoys self-modification, both in mundane forms like his tattoos, and magical transformations. He routinely visits the local Goblin Market in hopes of finding such means of self-improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T21:24:21-08:00","id":818189,"title":"","content":"I think Ziggy Zapf is an excellent example of a perfectly valid Beast that is neither feral nor predatory but still hits all the marks. Thanks for the contribution, BronzeDog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T21:36:18-08:00","id":818195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818159#post818159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be overly focused on the aesthetic idea of a feral child, since you are associating the Beast Seeming with it, when the only thing they both have in common is the appeal to wildness. The psychology of a Beast does not match the feral children. Like I said before, try Ogre or Elemental instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You can't do this because another one fits better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818159#post818159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem is that you're overly limiting and restricting character concepts to rigid stereotypes, and don't allow sufficient leeway for things to actually make sense. If your Keeper was a stereotypical patriarchal great white hunter, then you might see shades of him whenever a rich older white man speaks on TV. It makes quite a bit of sense if you are willing to imagine the situation and allow it to unfold to its logical conclusion instead of just fixating on a single specific thing and expecting everything to revolve around it. Not all Beasts are overtly feral or predatory. Some of them are skittish and fast, some are big and majestic, some are sleek and elegant, some are sharp and ornery, some are gentle until roused, and so on. The thing they all have in common is that they regain Clarity when they defy societal conventions, because it evokes how they escaped.<br /> <br /> Even the current text doesn't always reference predators or feral changelings. One of the examples is a changeling that digs his way out of his kennel. That's very non-confrontative, and yet it's also a defiance of social norms. You're not supposed to dig your way out of a cage. You're supposed to stay in there like the good tamed pet you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you just tell me how I can't do X because Y fits better? How is that not overly limiting and restricting character concepts and not allowing for leeway? I understand not all of them are predators, in fact that was one of my gripes. I do like the idea that some can be skittish, and some large and majestic, etc. It's just that many of the allusions presented don't give this impression.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818159#post818159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's fair or reasonable of you to expect all Beast changelings to behave the same way and have the same opinions regarding societal mores. Some may be happy merely ignoring them (some may do so rarely, others constantly), some may want to actively spit in the face of them. It's character diversity, and it's a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so why are you telling me that &quot;You're doing it wrong?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T21:44:31-08:00","id":818198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818195#post818195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You can't do this because another one fits better.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said you couldn't do anything. You're free to do whatever you want. I'm just solving your problem. If you want a feral changeling, you will find both the mechanics and fluff of Ogres or Elementals more suitable for your concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818195#post818195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't you just tell me how I can't do X because Y fits better? How is that not overly limiting and restricting character concepts and not allowing for leeway? I understand not all of them are predators, in fact that was one of my gripes. I do like the idea that some can be skittish, and some large and majestic, etc. It's just that many of the allusions presented don't give this impression.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are mixing up my addressing of your specific desire to play a feral changeling with my rebuttal of your general gripe with Beasts as a whole. I think that for the psychology of a feral changeling, the Beast Seeming is not the optimal choice. However, you are free to choose suboptimally. The points you are contending were my rebuttal to your dissatisfaction with the Beast Seeming as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818195#post818195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so why are you telling me that &quot;You're doing it wrong?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not telling you that you're doing it wrong, I'm telling you that you have an overly narrow view of something and that you're asking for things to change in order to better fit your vision, which is not terribly sympathetic towards people who like Beasts the way they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T21:54:58-08:00","id":818202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818198#post818198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said you couldn't do anything. You're free to do whatever you want. I'm just solving your problem. If you want a feral changeling, you will find both the mechanics and fluff of Ogres or Elementals more suitable for your concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading over Ogres and Elementals there are similarities, but they seem to be thematically different, at least from my reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T22:24:13-08:00","id":818208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818202#post818202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading over Ogres and Elementals there are similarities, but they seem to be thematically different, at least from my reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, and I think this is the root of the problem, is that you are assuming that you can determine a changeling's Seeming in a vacuum, without taking the time to imagine their Durance. An Ogre makes for a perfect feral child that lashes out when provoked, or that prioritises defending themselves from harm above all else. An Elemental fits the feral child that flees instead, or that withdraws into a fugue state or catatonia. And the Seeming emerges organically from the changeling's actions, so you can't examine it in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> The optimal way to analyse Seemings is to determine first what the changeling did in their Durance, and then figure out what Seeming fits that action best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T23:07:36-08:00","id":818226,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is that you're thinking in terms of archetype, and that's not what Seemings are about. Seemings are about how you took agency. They're about what you did to escape. They're about <i>action</i>. There is no &quot;feral child&quot; Seeming because feral child isn't an action, it's an archetype. There is no &quot;following your base instincts&quot; Seeming because following your instincts isn't an action, it's a motivation. Any Seeming can be motivated to escape due to instinct. Any Seeming can become a feral child when they return to the mortal world. What defines this feral child character's Seeming is <i>what his instincts drove him to do</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-30-2016, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T23:47:17-08:00","id":818242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818226#post818226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the problem is that you're thinking in terms of archetype, and that's not what Seemings are about. Seemings are about how you took agency. They're about what you did to escape. They're about <i>action</i>. There is no &quot;feral child&quot; Seeming because feral child isn't an action, it's an archetype. There is no &quot;following your base instincts&quot; isn't an action, it's a motivation. Any Seeming can be motivated to escape due to instinct. Any Seeming can become a feral child when they return to the mortal world. What defines this feral child character's Seeming is <i>what his instincts drove him to do</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's a bad habit from 1e then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T01:50:03-08:00","id":818291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818148#post818148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, how isn't being a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feral_child\" target=\"_blank\">feral child</a> psychology? The thing is that I guess I don't follow how someone goes from being screwed over by the Gentry to social justice warrior. The two tones seem to conflict quite heavily. Beast seems to be trying to pander to &quot;primal reversion&quot; and &quot;angsty rebel&quot; simultaneously and I don't really think it fits. Maybe it's not really trying to be the formal at all, but it certainly tries to pretend it is. I don't even know why they're called Beasts anyway, doesn't seem to really fit what they're supposed to be.<br /> <br /> I guess the problem with the tone is there's a difference between <b>ignoring</b> cultural norms, and actively <b>spitting in the face</b> of cultural norms. Beasts, in their current state, seem to do the latter. It's almost some mix of preachy and rebelling without a cause, and it really rubs me the wrong way.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm bringing this up, I think maybe it should be reevaluated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been evaluated and re-evaluated during the first and second draft passes. We disagree with your assertions. And we're way beyond making major tonal shifts eight months after the material was posted. <br /> <br /> I think you're taking an immensely reductive approach to this material - and one that seems heavily biased by the use of very specific fad terminology you're projecting on how you think we expect people to play - and I do hope that others' input can help you to approach it more generously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T02:17:39-08:00","id":818300,"title":"","content":"One thing I like about seemings is that while the escape strongly defines your bond with the faery, it doesn't necessarily directly affect your personality. That it's more subtle than &quot;Okay you escaped through breaking a convention and expectation so now your constantly rebelling&quot;, instead encouraging and discouraging behaviours through clarity.<br /> <br /> One of the chains that binds humanity is that you can't just do what your instincts tell you to, but knowing that &quot;Wait, if I do act on my instincts I'll be more grounded.&quot; means there is more reason to act on your instincts so you just end up doing it more. But you'll also want to be tied down less, not because &quot;Fey magic says so&quot; but because such experiences remind you of your durance and increase the grip the faery has on your perceptions. <br /> <br /> Just thought I should say that I greatly enjoy the subtly and finesse in getting the mechanics to influence the players rather than ordering the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:28:37-08:00","id":818379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818291#post818291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been evaluated and re-evaluated during the first and second draft passes. We disagree with your assertions. And we're way beyond making major tonal shifts eight months after the material was posted.<br /> <br /> I think you're taking an immensely reductive approach to this material - and one that seems heavily biased by the use of very specific fad terminology you're projecting on how you think we expect people to play - and I do hope that others' input can help you to approach it more generously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize, then, that's just what I have taken away from the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:32:43-08:00","id":818382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/817610-thoughts-on-the-beast-preview?p=818379#post818379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I apologize, then, that's just what I have taken away from the material.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all cool. No worries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}